    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d799">

                <pb facs="0983" n="975" xml:id="pg975"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867N.01/1215: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Jerusalem</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wadsworth</hi>)<anchor n="97"
                        xml:id="d799-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-10-27T19:00:00-05:00">October 27, 1938—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your telegram of October 25, 6 p.m. It is suggested that, in your discretion, you
                    might properly acquaint responsible Arab as well as Jewish inquirers with the
                    Department’s public statement concerning Palestine.<anchor n="98"
                        xml:id="d799-f2"/> Should you deem it desirable, you may explain also that
                    the statement represents no change in this Government’s position with respect to
                    that question. (See, in this connection, Department’s Radio Bulletin No.
                    244.)</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d799-f1" n="97" type="source" xml:id="d799-f1-content">
                <p>A similar telegram was sent on the same date to the Minister Resident In Iraq as
                    No. 21.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d799-f2" n="98" xml:id="d799-f2-content">
                <p>Press release of October 14, <ref target="#pg953">p. 953</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
